E["npc:loganaar"] = {t="npc",n="Loganaar",z="moonglade",s="In Nighthaven, Loganaar guides druids from both factions in the ways of their calling. He teaches them to heed nature and prepares them for the Emerald Dream.",h="In Nighthaven, Loganaar guides druids from both factions in the ways of their calling.",sec={{t="Keeper of the Sacred Art",b="Loganaar welcomes newly initiated druids who come to Moonglade from Darnassus or Thunder Bluff. In Nighthaven, he teaches balance, shape-shifting, and reverence for nature. Even in cold stone or unfamiliar lands, he says, tranquility must come from within. He also leads promising students toward deeper Cenarion Circle concerns.\n\nSome druids he sends to wanderers such as Torwa Pathfinder in Un'Goro Crater. Others he guides into ancient woodland rites.",sp=0},{t="The Call of the Dream",b="Loganaar teaches that Kalimdor's traditional protectors share a deeper calling: the Emerald Dream. He speaks of the sacred bond between Azeroth's primal spirit realm and the waking world. To master their path, druids must hibernate for centuries and walk among nature's purest forms, guided by the demigods.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Loganaar?",a="Loganaar guides druids in Nighthaven, Moonglade's central settlement. He welcomes druids from every background and introduces them to the Cenarion Circle's deeper traditions.",al={"loganaar npc","who is loganaar","loganaar lore"}},{q="Does Loganaar train Horde druids?",a="Yes. Loganaar teaches both tauren and night elf druids. As a member of the Cenarion Circle, he sets aside the conflict between the Alliance and Horde on Moonglade's sacred, neutral ground.",al={"can tauren train at loganaar","loganaar horde","druid trainer moonglade horde"}},{q="What does Loganaar teach about the Emerald Dream?",a="Loganaar teaches that every true druid feels the Emerald Dream's pull. He says a long, deep hibernation lets druids walk among its uncorrupted forms, where their ultimate training takes place.",al={"loganaar dream","emerald dream quote"}},{q="Where does Loganaar send seasoned druids?",a="Loganaar sends seasoned druids to observe and mend Azeroth's primal ecosystems. He directs some to help naturalists such as Torwa Pathfinder in the wilderness of Un'Goro Crater.",al={"loganaar quests","torwa pathfinder quest loganaar"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid of Darnassus or Thunder Bluff, you meet Loganaar early after teleporting to Moonglade. He offers advanced training and spiritual counsel.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you share the Kaldorei druids' ancient traditions. For millennia, they communed with nature and entered the Emerald Dream under Malfurion Stormrage."},kw={"cenarion circle","druid trainer","emerald dream","loganaar","moonglade","nighthaven"},rel={"subzone:nighthaven","zone:moonglade","topic:druid","topic:emerald-dream","npc:torwa-pathfinder","topic:cenarius","topic:night-elf"},src={"Loganaar"}}
E["npc:remulos"] = {t="npc",n="Remulos",z="moonglade",s="In Moonglade, Keeper Remulos guides the druids of the Cenarion Circle. Cenarius has fallen and Malfurion Stormrage sleeps, so Remulos helps lead the Circle. He puts nature’s balance before night elven isolation.",h="In Moonglade, Keeper Remulos guides the druids of the Cenarion Circle.",sec={{t="Lord of the Sacred Grove",b="Keeper Remulos watches over Moonglade, the druids’ sacred sanctuary north of Mount Hyjal. Immortal, he bears the lower body of a great stag and the antlered torso of an ancient dryad-father. His divine authority and counsel aid the Cenarion Circle while Malfurion Stormrage remains trapped in the Emerald Dream. He works to heal Azeroth’s scars and aids druids in their sacred rites around Lake Elune'ara.",sp=0},{t="A Rift in the Circle",b="Keeper Remulos often clashes with Archdruid Fandral Staghelm over the Circle’s path. Staghelm champions night elven supremacy and sought to restore his people’s lost immortality by planting Teldrassil. Remulos opposed the new World Tree, seeing its planting as hubris.\n\nRemulos also defied Staghelm’s isolationist faction by welcoming Hamuul Runetotem and the tauren into the Cenarion Circle. There, their shamans-turned-druids could learn nature’s closely guarded mysteries and help restore the land alongside others.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Keeper Remulos?",a="Keeper Remulos is an immortal son of Cenarius and brother to the fallen Zaetar. He lives in the Shrine of Remulos in Moonglade, guards the grove, and is a senior leader of the Cenarion Circle.",al={"remulos lore","who is remulos","keeper remulos background"}},{q="Why does Remulos support the tauren druids?",a="Remulos believes nature’s balance reaches beyond mortal racial divides. He recognized the tauren’s deep bond with the Earth Mother and welcomed Archdruid Hamuul Runetotem and his people into the Cenarion Circle despite Archdruid Fandral Staghelm’s objections.",al={"remulos tauren","why do tauren have druids","remulos hamuul"}},{q="What is Remulos's opinion on Teldrassil?",a="Remulos vehemently opposed the creation of Teldrassil. He saw the planting of the new World Tree as a selfish attempt by night elves to reclaim their lost immortality, not a true effort to heal Azeroth.",al={"remulos world tree","remulos fandral tree"}},{q="What relation does Remulos have to Maraudon?",a="Remulos’s brother Zaetar ventured into Desolace and mated with Princess Theradras, becoming the father of the centaur before his death. Remulos warned Zaetar against the union, and Maraudon holds his brother’s legacy and that of the centaur.",al={"remulos zaetar","remulos theradras","remulos brother"},sp=1}},ang={["class:Druid"]="Whether night elf or tauren, every druid journeys to Moonglade to meet Keeper Remulos and seek guidance in mastering animal forms and sacred trials.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren druid, you can revere Remulos for defying Fandral Staghelm and welcoming your people into the Cenarion Circle, where they received full teaching."},kw={"cenarion circle","cenarius","fandral staghelm","grove","hamuul runetotem","moonglade","remulos","zaetar"},rel={"topic:cenarion-circle","topic:cenarius","zone:moonglade","npc:fandral-staghelm","quest:1489","npc:malfurion-stormrage","subzone:lake-elune-ara","topic:druid"},src={"Keeper Remulos"}}
E["subzone:lake-elune-ara"] = {t="subzone",n="Lake Elune'ara",z="moonglade",s="At Moonglade's heart, Lake Elune'ara rests beneath moonlit groves. The sacred waters honor Elune, and the Cenarion Circle's shrine grounds border its shores.",h="At Moonglade's heart, Lake Elune'ara rests beneath moonlit groves.",sec={{t="Heart of the Sacred Vale",b="Moonlit groves frame Lake Elune'ara, whose waters are said to bear the White Lady's blessing. Nighthaven lies to the north, and the Cenarion Circle's shrine grounds border the lake. Initiates have long searched its depths for lost relics. Through contact with nature's currents, they seek harmony with the land.",sp=0},{t="The Slumber of Omen",b="Ancient peril sleeps beneath Lake Elune'ara's quiet surface. Legends tell of Omen, a two-headed wolf demigod and revered ancient corrupted by the Burning Legion during the War of the Ancients. Defeated long ago, Omen was cast into the lake bed. There he sleeps beneath the dark water, a reminder of nature's wounds.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Lake Elune'ara?",a="Night elves and druids revere Lake Elune'ara's sacred waters at the heart of Moonglade. Its name honors the Moon Goddess Elune, and the Cenarion Circle's sanctuaries surround it.",al={"lake eluneara","moonglade lake","where is lake eluneara"}},{q="What lurks at the bottom of the lake?",a="Omen, a fallen demigod, sleeps in the lake's dark depths. Once a noble ancient, he was driven mad by the Burning Legion during the ancient war and cast into the lake after his defeat.",al={"what is inside lake elune'ara","omen in moonglade","monster in lake"}},{q="Why do druids come to this lake?",a="Druids come to the lake for trials and to commune with the spirits of nature. Young druids search its waters for sacred relics as part of their rites of passage.",al={"druid quest lake","aquatic form lake"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you know Lake Elune'ara as a place for rituals and trials. Sacred relics in its deep waters aid initiates on their path.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you know Lake Elune'ara by its name, which honors Elune. The lake is a place of divine peace and recalls the War of the Ancients."},kw={"cenarion circle","dark waters","elune","lake elune'ara","moonglade","nighthaven","omen"},rel={"zone:moonglade","topic:druid","topic:elune","quest:31","topic:emerald-dream","quest:5921"},src={"Lake Elune'ara"}}
E["subzone:nighthaven"] = {t="subzone",n="Nighthaven",z="moonglade",s="Nighthaven welcomes druids of both factions to Moonglade’s northern shore. Night elves and tauren study together in peace at the Cenarion Circle’s heart.",h="Nighthaven welcomes druids of both factions to Moonglade’s northern shore.",sec={{t="A Sanctuary of the Cenarion Circle",b="Along Lake Elune'ara’s calm northern shore, Nighthaven gathers night elf halls and moonwells among its groves. The Cenarion Circle keeps this secluded village as a place for druids to learn and tend to nature. Trainers, herbalists, and suppliers serve those who come to study. Here, druids find neutral ground whatever their ties to the Alliance or the Horde.",sp=0},{t="Ancient History and Sacred Gatherings",b="Peace in Nighthaven has faced a trial. Centuries after the War of the Ancients, champions gathered there to face the enraged demigod Omen. They drove him beneath Lake Elune'ara. During the Lunar Festival, the village opens its borders to pilgrims from across Azeroth, who honor the ancestors beneath Elune's watchful gaze.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who rules or oversees Nighthaven?",a="The Cenarion Circle oversees Nighthaven, guided by Keeper Remulos and senior druids such as Loganaar. The village is an independent, neutral sanctuary, outside the night elven government’s rule.",al={"who runs nighthaven","nighthaven leaders","who is in charge here"}},{q="Can non-druids visit Nighthaven?",a="Yes. Non-druids can reach Moonglade through the Timbermaw tunnels or by taking a public flight to elsewhere in the valley, then travel to Nighthaven. The village’s own flight masters serve druids only.",al={"can non druids go to nighthaven","how do non druids get here"}},{q="Why are night elves and tauren living together peacefully here?",a="Night elves and tauren live peacefully in Nighthaven because the Cenarion Circle places healing nature and the Emerald Dream above faction politics. Its members vow to remain neutral in Moonglade and study druidism as equals, setting aside Alliance and Horde rivalries.",al={"why no fighting here","why are tauren allowed here","horde alliance peace"}},{q="What flight routes are available from Nighthaven?",a="Druids can take direct routes with Nighthaven’s Cenarion flight masters. Alliance druids can fly by hippogryph to Rut'theran Village, while Horde druids can ride wind riders to Thunder Bluff.",al={"nighthaven flight masters","where can i fly from here"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you find your spiritual home in Moonglade at Nighthaven. Teleport: Moonglade brings you to your order's mentors, animal form trials, and flight connections to Rut'theran Village or Thunder Bluff.",["profession:Herbalism"]="As an herbalist, you can consult herbalism trainers among Nighthaven's tranquil groves in Moonglade."},kw={"cenarion circle","druid","lake elune'ara","loganaar","lunar festival","moonglade","nighthaven","remulos"},rel={"zone:moonglade","topic:cenarion-circle","subzone:lake-elune-ara","npc:remulos","npc:loganaar","topic:druid","subzone:rut-theran-village","zone:thunderbluff"},src={"Nighthaven"}}
E["subzone:stormrage-barrow-dens"] = {t="subzone",n="Stormrage Barrow Dens",z="moonglade",s="Beneath Moonglade, druids sleep in the Stormrage Barrow Dens. Their bodies rest here while their spirits journey through the Emerald Dream.",h="Beneath Moonglade, druids sleep in the Stormrage Barrow Dens.",sec={{t="Chambers of the Slumbering",b="Beneath Moonglade, the Stormrage Barrow Dens hold druids in deep sleep. Barrow dens across night elven lands guard their bodies while their spirits journey through the Emerald Dream. These earthen halls bear the name of Archdruid Malfurion Stormrage. Clintar Dreamwalker still sleeps in one of their alcoves. Malfurion is absent, and his brethren keep watch over the quiet chambers.",sp=0},{t="Echoes of the Third War",b="The Stormrage Barrow Dens nearly fell during the Third War. Tichondrius and the Burning Legion sought to destroy the sleeping druids before they could rally. High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind fought demons and corrupted wildlife in the tunnels, then sounded the Horn of Cenarius. The call woke Malfurion Stormrage in time. After Archimonde fell at Mount Hyjal, Malfurion's spirit returned to the Emerald Dream. His brethren still watch over the dens.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the Stormrage Barrow Dens?",a="Barrow dens shelter night elf druids while they journey through the Emerald Dream. Their bodies lie still and unguarded for months or years, so their brethren keep watch over these quiet underground sanctuaries.",al={"what are the barrow dens for","why sleep in barrow dens","stormrage barrow dens purpose"}},{q="Is Malfurion Stormrage currently inside these dens?",a="Malfurion Stormrage is absent from the dens. He slept there during the Third War, until Tyrande awakened him. Since the war, his spirit has been lost in the Emerald Dream, and the Cenarion Circle carries on without him.",al={"where is malfurion","is malfurion in the barrow dens","can i find malfurion here"}},{q="Who is currently sleeping within these dens?",a="Clintar Dreamwalker is among the druids sleeping in the dens. His body rests beneath the earth while his spirit journeys through nature's pathways.",al={"who is asleep here","clintar dreamwalker","sleeping druids moonglade"}},{q="What happened to this place during the Third War?",a="During the Third War, Tichondrius and the Burning Legion invaded the dens to kill the sleeping night elf druids. High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind fought through the demons and sounded the Horn of Cenarius, waking Malfurion.",al={"third war barrow dens","tichondrius attack moonglade","tyrande awakening of stormrage"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you see the Stormrage Barrow Dens as a heart of Cenarion heritage. Elder druids shelter their bodies in the earth while their spirits journey through the Emerald Dream.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you remember the long watch over the sleeping druids and Tyrande Whisperwind's perilous descent to awaken Malfurion against the Burning Legion."},kw={"barrow den","cenarion circle","clintar dreamwalker","emerald dream","malfurion","moonglade","stormrage barrow dens"},rel={"zone:moonglade","npc:malfurion-stormrage","topic:emerald-dream","topic:cenarion-circle","topic:druid","npc:tyrande-whisperwind","topic:third-war","topic:night-elf"},src={"Stormrage Barrow Dens"}}
E["subzone:timbermaw-hold"] = {t="subzone",n="Timbermaw Hold",z="moonglade",s="Within Timbermaw Hold, a furbolg tribe still resists demonic corruption. Its tunnels link Felwood, Moonglade, and Winterspring.",h="Within Timbermaw Hold, a furbolg tribe still resists demonic corruption.",sec={{t="A Sanctuary Amidst Decay",b="Deep beneath the mountain, the Timbermaw guard their home while corruption spreads through the forests above. During the Third War, the Burning Legion tainted neighboring furbolg tribes, but the Timbermaw endured in these stone corridors. From below, they watched their beloved forests warp. Now they distrust outsiders and defend every tunnel entrance, expecting violence from anyone coming in from the infected woods.",sp=0},{t="Crossroads of the North",b="Timbermaw Hold is the only direct passage through the mountain between Felwood, Moonglade, and Winterspring. Its sentries let outsiders pass only after they prove their goodwill. Those who oppose the corrupted furbolg clans may find steadfast allies among the Timbermaw. They share their ancient shamanic knowledge and leathercrafting traditions.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why do the furbolgs in Timbermaw Hold attack visitors?",a="The Timbermaw distrust outsiders after seeing neighboring kin succumb to the Burning Legion’s corruption. They fear strangers may bring the taint into their home or be mistaken for feral, demonic furbolgs. So they attack until visitors prove peaceful intentions.",al={"why are timbermaw hostile","timbermaw attacking me","how to get timbermaw friendly"}},{q="Which zones does Timbermaw Hold connect?",a="Timbermaw Hold connects Felwood, Moonglade, and Winterspring. Its main cavern opens to northern Felwood in the southwest, Moonglade to the north, and Winterspring to the east. A walled-off gate also lies in northern Azshara.",al={"timbermaw hold tunnel destinations","where does timbermaw hold lead","timbermaw exits"}},{q="How did the Timbermaw survive the Legion's taint?",a="The Timbermaw sheltered deep in their mountain caverns while demonic fel energy withered Felwood’s forests. During the height of the demonic invasion, they sealed themselves inside the hold. This preserved their minds and sacred shamanic ways while neighboring clans fell to madness.",al={"why are timbermaw uncorrupted","timbermaw not corrupted"}},{q="What is the sealed wooden door inside the hold?",a="A round wooden barrier blocks a side cavern deeper in the tunnels. Its purpose is uncertain, though travelers think it may seal older tunnel complexes leading toward the Barrow Deeps or other ancient chambers beneath Mount Hyjal.",al={"blocked door in timbermaw hold","timbermaw hold locked gate"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you can travel through the hold between your sacred sanctuary in Moonglade and wounded Felwood. Furbolg spirits there need cleansing.",["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you can see how the Timbermaw have kept their spiritual traditions and healing rituals uncorrupted despite the fel corruption outside their cave gates."},kw={"felwood","furbolg","moonglade","timbermaw","timbermaw hold","tunnel","winterspring"},rel={"topic:furbolg","zone:felwood","zone:winterspring","zone:moonglade","topic:burning-legion","zone:azshara","subzone:irontree-woods"},src={"Timbermaw Hold"}}
E["zone:moonglade"] = {t="zone",n="Moonglade",z="moonglade",s="In Moonglade, druids of the Cenarion Circle gather beneath an endless twilight. The valley in northern Kalimdor shelters night elf and tauren druids, while travelers on foot brave Timbermaw Hold to reach it.",h="In Moonglade, druids of the Cenarion Circle gather beneath an endless twilight.",sec={{t="Sacred Twilight",b="Moonglade lies among the mountains north of Felwood and Winterspring. Beneath Elune's moon, twilight lingers over Lake Elune'ara, at the heart of a valley sacred since kaldorei civilization began. The Burning Legion left the glade untouched in both its ancient invasions and the recent Third War, held back by Cenarius and his offspring. Keeper Remulos watches over Moonglade now, guarding nature's balance in a refuge where factional conflict has no place.",sp=0},{t="Seat of the Circle",b="Malfurion Stormrage founded the Cenarion Circle millennia ago, and Moonglade remains its headquarters. In lakeside Nighthaven, druids learn from ancient traditions. After the Third War, the Circle welcomed tauren into its ranks, following Archdruid Hamuul Runetotem's teachings. Here, Alliance and Horde loyalties are set aside. Armed sentries keep the peace, and members who turn to violence face swift justice.",sp=0},{t="The Barrow Dens and the Dream",b="South of Lake Elune'ara lie the Stormrage Barrow Dens. For thousands of years, elven druids slept in these underground hollows as their spirits crossed the Emerald Dream. Their bodies rested under constant watch. During the Third War, Tyrande Whisperwind sounded the Horn of Cenarius here and awakened Malfurion.\n\nThe dens remain tied to the Dream. Yet strange ripples now rise from their deep tunnels, and dark whispers trouble the Emerald realm.",sp=1}},faq={{q="How do non-druid travelers reach Moonglade?",a="On foot, you pass through Timbermaw Hold, a tunnel complex linking upper Felwood, Winterspring, and Moonglade, unless ritual magic brings you during seasonal events. Timbermaw furbolgs guard the passage fiercely, and outsiders must prove their goodwill to earn safe conduct.",al={"how to get to moonglade","getting to moonglade","moonglade entrance"}},{q="Why can Horde and Alliance walk together peacefully here?",a="The Cenarion Circle governs Moonglade, serving nature rather than politics. Moonglade Wardens throughout Nighthaven attack anyone who starts violence against those in good standing with the Circle.",al={"why is moonglade neutral","pvp in moonglade","can horde and alliance fight here"}},{q="What is the purpose of Nighthaven?",a="Nighthaven is Moonglade's main settlement, where the Cenarion Circle dwells and works. Trainers, caretakers, and sanctuaries give kaldorei and tauren druids places to confer about the health of Azeroth's wild lands.",al={"nighthaven purpose","what is nighthaven","town in moonglade"}},{q="Who rules Moonglade in Malfurion Stormrage's absence?",a="Keeper Remulos watches over Moonglade from the Shrine of Remulos while Malfurion Stormrage is absent. With senior Circle members such as Dendrite Starblaze, he tends the sacred grounds and directs efforts to heal the world.",al={"leader of moonglade","who leads cenarion circle","who is remulos"}},{q="What rests beneath the Stormrage Barrow Dens?",a="The Stormrage Barrow Dens are deep chambers where druids entered long communion with the Emerald Dream. Their deep wings still hold powerful conduits to the Dream, though recent disturbances suggest unsettling nightmares are stirring within.",al={"barrow dens lore","stormrage barrow dens purpose","where druids sleep"}},{q="Why do druids have special flight paths out of Nighthaven?",a="Silva Fil'naveth, the hippogryph master, and Bunthen Plainswind, the wind rider keeper, offer druids direct passage from Nighthaven to Rut'theran Village and Thunder Bluff. These routes help the order travel between its sacred grove and its racial homelands.",al={"nighthaven flight masters","druid flight master moonglade","free flights in moonglade"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, Moonglade is your sacred home and sanctuary. Your spiritual bond lets you teleport here from anywhere across Azeroth, consult masters like Dendrite Starblaze, commune with great spirits, and master forms such as aquatic form.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, your place in the Cenarion Circle renews an ancient bond with Cenarius. Hamuul Runetotem championed your inclusion, which Moonglade honors despite the night elves' long seclusion.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, Moonglade was your people's spiritual heartland for ten millennia and the resting place of your sleeping archdruids. Elune's enduring blessing sheltered it."},kw={"cenarion circle","dendrite starblaze","emerald dream","lake elune'ara","moonglade","nighthaven","remulos","stormrage barrow dens"},rel={"topic:cenarion-circle","topic:druid","npc:remulos","subzone:nighthaven","subzone:stormrage-barrow-dens","subzone:lake-elune-ara","topic:emerald-dream","subzone:timbermaw-hold"},src={"Moonglade"}}
